WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.664
Think about your local bakery. The owner wants profit. The bakers want fair pay. Customers want fresh bread at a good price. Neighbours want no noise or mess. All of these people care about what the bakery does.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:29.586
Each of these people or groups is called a stakeholder. A stakeholder is any person or group that is affected by, or has an interest in, what a business does.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:42.141
Now think about a large company. It is split into small pieces of ownership called shares. Anyone who owns one or more shares in a company is a shareholder, so they are a part-owner.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:54.507
So every shareholder is a stakeholder, because owners care about the business. But not every stakeholder is a shareholder. A customer cares about the business but does not own it.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:01:05.559
Step one: decide which term the question asks for. Stakeholder and shareholder look alike, so read the word carefully.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:16.269
Step two: for stakeholder, give the meaning: a person or group with an interest in, or affected by, the business. The interest link earns the mark.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:27.100
Step three: for shareholder, say it is a person or organisation that owns shares in a company. The word own is what earns the mark.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:36.083
Step four: you may add one short example, but the meaning always comes first. An example on its own is not a definition.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:46.866
Here is a real question from Paper one in November 2020. Define the term stakeholder. It is worth one mark.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:57.126
The command is define, so give the meaning in one sentence. A stakeholder is any person or group that is affected by, or has an interest in, the activities of a business.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:07.901
Then add a short example to show you understand, such as its employees, customers or the local community. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:18.348
The most common mistake is saying a stakeholder is someone who owns the business. That describes a shareholder or an owner.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:27.715
Another mistake is being vague. A shareholder is not just someone who invests. Say clearly that they own shares in a company.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:46.019
Now you try. Define the term shareholder. Then decide: is a business that supplies plastic to a toy company, and owns no shares in it, a stakeholder, a shareholder, or both? Pause and decide.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:03:03.304
A shareholder is a person or organisation that owns one or more shares in a company. The supplier is a stakeholder, because the toy company's orders affect its sales. It is not a shareholder, because it owns no shares.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:15.283
Remember the method: decide which term is asked, give its meaning in one sentence, then add one short example. Now try the practice questions for this type.
